Carafe Lab: a control channel for one Eden that runs a whole set. With CARAFE_CONTROL naming a folder, Eden reads
a one-line `command` file there every 200 ms and removes it: `boot <file>` starts software, `stop` closes it the
way the HOME menu does and keeps Eden open, `screenshot <file>` saves the exact picture the renderer draws, `quit`
stops and closes Eden. Every answer is a numbered line appended to `replies`: `ready`, `booting`, `booted`,
`capturing`, `stopped exited|forced|immediately|self|idle`, or `error …`.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

